<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Comrades: Almost a Love Story (film, Peter Chan)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1996</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the film's Chinese title and a recurring song in it</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Day I Met You (Teresa Teng)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1980</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Cantonese version, words by Lo Kwak-chan</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Tian Mi Mi (Luhan)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2015</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover for the film's mainland release</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Covers by Faye Wong, Stephen Chow, Leon Lai, Yu Quan and Jane Zhang</span><span class="sg-chain-h">covers</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Dayung Sampan (Dasimah)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1940s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new Mandarin words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Dayung Sampan (Teresa Teng, Indonesian-language cover)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1978</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Teng's earlier recording of the melody</span></li></ul></section>
